{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310837,"nonce":"uxMwz4KnWXHsTqqlbXlARTfCOP0=","title":"L3 DONE 2026-09-05 (adapters shipped; typed-vs-erased `get` box kind still open). Was: L3 implementation plan (from the 2026-09-05 D12 ...","message":"**Landed:** commits 72b574b4 (devirt env) af61b4fb (map slot adapters) edd52081 (KeyValueIterator protocol) a7c1041c (erased Null\u003cT\u003e boundaries) 721e10d0 (typer IMap identity); battery 439/439 vs conf_d9c, GAINED Issue3635 / LOST Issue12700 both bistable on one binary (12700: 2/5 PASS).\n\n`wrap_in_interface_fat_ptr` when the class has a runtime-mapping row for the slot's method; var-init\nwrap no longer requires a pre-registered (class, iface) vtable. The adapters were CORRECT from the\nfirst build; the three crashes that followed were the devirtualizer env bug, the typeless IntMap\nplaceholder, and the `Null\u003cV\u003e` box at the erased boundary (see the linked notes). OPEN: `get`\nboxes as an INT box for any V (H-B-style gap) — a typed V=String/Float/Bool caller through IMap\ngets the wrong box.\n\nPrereq: L1 landed (5c42a916 subtype resolver; interface kind fix-up in flight) so\n`(StringMap, IMap)` vtables exist and `RAYZOR_IFACE_DIAG=1` prints `[fatptr]` slots\n(today: 10 slots, only `keyValueIterator` resolved; the rest are empty by-name\nstubs `__vtable_dispatch_thunk__haxe_ds_StringMap_\u003cm\u003e` that trap).\n\n**Builder:** `ensure_extern_mapped_dispatch_thunk(class_fqn, method, key, call,\nvkind, class_sym, iface_sym)` in `compiler/src/ir/mir/decl/vtables.rs`, sibling of\n`ensure_vtable_dispatch_thunk`. `enum ExternValueKind { Erased, I32, F64, Bool, Ref }`\nfrom the receiver's last type arg (mirror stdlib_runtime.rs:487-505); inside\nStringMap.keyValueIterator (`this: StringMap\u003cT\u003e`) it is Erased = the g4a path.\nCache `(class_fqn, method, vkind) -\u003e IrFunctionId` next to `vtable_dispatch_thunks`;\ninsert BEFORE building the body (copy re-wraps). NAME: for Erased exactly\n`__vtable_dispatch_thunk__\u003csanitize(class_fqn.method)\u003e` so an earlier module's\nempty by-name stub DEDUPES with the real body at merge (helpers/vtables.rs:239-242);\ntyped kinds append `__i32/__f64/__bool/__ref`. Signature `(env:*u8, this:*void,\nargs...) -\u003e ret`, Haxe CC, FunctionKind::UserDefined (NOT MirWrapper). Body via the\nsave/restore choreography of vtables.rs:181-268. Erased K/V params are I64.\n\n**Per slot** (this = raw map ptr; K: StringMap `cast I64-\u003ePtr(String)`, IntMap\n`I64-\u003eI32-\u003eI64` extend, ObjectMap `bitcast I64-\u003eU64`):\n- get(k): `exists` probe -\u003e branch; true: `raw:U64 = haxe_*_get`; box by kind: I32\n  `haxe_box_int_ptr(cast U64-\u003eI64)`, F64 `haxe_box_float_ptr(bitcast)`, Bool\n  `haxe_box_bool_ptr`, Ref `bitcast U64-\u003ePtr(U8)` (unboxed; raw 0 = null), Erased\n  `haxe_box_int_ptr` (erased consumers unbox via haxe_unbox_int_ptr /\n  haxe_unbox_scalar_or_addr, bit-faithful). NOT haxe_box_typed_ptr (fixups never run\n  over the thunk), NOT haxe_box_reference_ptr (unbox_int returns 0).\n- set(k, v): V -\u003e raw u64 per kind as stdlib_runtime.rs:284-311; call; void.\n- exists/remove -\u003e Bool; clear -\u003e void; toString -\u003e String (*HaxeString).\n- keys()/iterator(): call the mir_wrapper (`stringmap_keys_iterator`, forward ref\n  `[Ptr(Void)] =\u003e Ptr(Void)`) THEN `build_iter_handle(it, \u0026IterSource::StdlibIterator\n  { has_next: \"ArrayIterator_hasNext\", next: \"ArrayIterator_next\", both is_mir })` and\n  return the HANDLE — a bare ArrayIterator's word 0 is 0, the consumer's tag check\n  fails silently (n=0). Same rule as `wrap_stdlib_iter_result` (D4).\n- keyValueIterator: NO adapter (real body; FQN fallback resolves it).\n- copy: ObjectMap has `haxe_objectmap_copy` -\u003e wrap result as a fat pointer in-thunk;\n  StringMap/IntMap have NO runtime copy -\u003e add runtime fns + rows, or keep the\n  trapping by-name stub. Never leave a slot unfilled (call sites index by count).\n\n**Selection:** in `wrap_in_interface_fat_ptr` (interfaces.rs:140-205) thread the\nreceiver TypeId in (all 6 callers have it), compute vkind once; BEFORE the\nfunc_id_opt resolution: `stdlib_mapping.class_key(class_fqn)` + `find_by_name(key,\nmname)` non-static non-ctor row -\u003e the adapter (a mapping row is authoritative over a\ncompiled body). Same check in `wrap_new_class_as_interface_by_name` (vkind Erased).\n\n**Holes the refuters found (must be closed in the same unit):** (H-A) if\n`map.get(key)` stays Dynamic-typed in MapKeyValueIterator.next, the `(… : V)` cast\ngoes through `haxe_std_downcast(box, tast_id)` which compares box.type_id by\nhierarchy — a TYPE_INT box vs V's id may fail: check the post-L1 TAST type of\n`map.get(key)` first. (H-B) `Iterator\u003cK\u003e` returned through an interface slot must\nbe a handle (above). (H-C) SRA drops field stores of an INLINED ctor in a same-file\nmirror (`RAYZOR_NO_SRA=1` fixes) — verify g4a with and without SRA.\nProbes: harness g4a/g4b; scratchpad/imap_l2b, imap_l2c (field/return-typed IMap);\nwf2_refute/ctl.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_imap_extern_map_slot_adapters_plan` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}